(532570, 51484, 4007, '<td valign="top">A great scene for a shot.  The trees are a little distracting but it was worth having them in the way in order to capture the mud path running in front of the building as well.</td>', 'A great scene for a shot.  The trees are a little distracting but it was worth having them in the way in order to capture the mud path running in front of the building as well.', '2004-01-05 15:09:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(532571, 51560, 10848, '<td valign="top">This is very interesting in the fact that you ventured from the normal wood colored dark shots that seem to be the way most capture a shot like this. The green in the guitar and the detail gives this shot that little extra that makes it orginal and stand out to me I like it good job</td>', 'This is very interesting in the fact that you ventured from the normal wood colored dark shots that seem to be the way most capture a shot like this. The green in the guitar and the detail gives this shot that little extra that makes it orginal and stand out to me I like it good job', '2004-01-05 15:10:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(532572, 53054, 4007, '<td valign="top">This is a nice simple shot that has a lot of character to it.  You might have experimented with going even wider on this shot in order to maximize the impact of the streetlamp''s pyramid of light it casts.  Good work.</td>', 'This is a nice simple shot that has a lot of character to it.  You might have experimented with going even wider on this shot in order to maximize the impact of the streetlamp''s pyramid of light it casts.  Good work.', '2004-01-05 15:10:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(532573, 52563, 4007, '<td valign="top">Hmm.  I''d be somewhat sad to discover that the star of light on the end of that drip was digitally added.  So I''m voting like it was real and hoping it''s true, because that really is the a nice touch to the shot, but it would seem like a cheep trick if it were purely post-production.<br/>Update: Glad to have heard that the star is legit.  I hope this shot scores well (and doesn''t get marked down from others having the same suspicions I had.)</td>', 'Hmm.  I''d be somewhat sad to discover that the star of light on the end of that drip was digitally added.  So I''m voting like it was real and hoping it''s true, because that really is the a nice touch to the shot, but it would seem like a cheep trick if it were purely post-production.Update: Glad to have heard that the star is legit.  I hope this shot scores well (and doesn''t get marked down from others having the same suspicions I had.)', '2004-01-05 15:12:09.000000', NULL, 1),
