(538506, 52276, 9906, '<td valign="top">I really am starting to appreciate the shots that you can''t really tell if they''re B/W (duotone) or color with very little color.  Nice feeling of depth and simplicity!<br/>TC</td>', 'I really am starting to appreciate the shots that you can''t really tell if they''re B/W (duotone) or color with very little color.  Nice feeling of depth and simplicity!TC', '2004-01-11 00:11:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(538507, 52964, 9906, '<td valign="top">Lighting is a little harsh here.  A different time of day may help with that issue.  Also I think that you need a little fill lighitng as it''s hard to tell where subject ends and tree begins.<br/>TC</td>', 'Lighting is a little harsh here.  A different time of day may help with that issue.  Also I think that you need a little fill lighitng as it''s hard to tell where subject ends and tree begins.TC', '2004-01-11 00:15:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(538508, 50104, 9906, '<td valign="top">This seems a little flat (the bike itself) and dull.  I think that fill lighting would help with the dull, not sure how to fix the flat part.<br/>TC</td>', 'This seems a little flat (the bike itself) and dull.  I think that fill lighting would help with the dull, not sure how to fix the flat part.TC', '2004-01-11 00:17:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(538509, 49898, 9906, '<td valign="top">When he''s older you can use this against him!!! (wink)<br/>TC</td>', 'When he''s older you can use this against him!!! (wink)TC', '2004-01-11 00:19:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(538510, 52558, 5475, '<td valign="top">I love the concept... the repetitious curves are wonderful.  The BW /  muted colors work well, although the yellows in the guitar are a little less saturated than I would have taken them (just personal preference, not a negative thing).  The only thing that really bugs me here is the certificate inside the guitar.<br/>JD</td>', 'I love the concept... the repetitious curves are wonderful.  The BW /  muted colors work well, although the yellows in the guitar are a little less saturated than I would have taken them (just personal preference, not a negative thing).  The only thing that really bugs me here is the certificate inside the guitar.JD', '2004-01-11 00:23:21.000000', NULL, 1),
