(1075941, 52895, 14986, '<td valign="top">What a great capture of this guy!  How close were you?  I would have cropped it vertically and blurred the background some to isolate the owl a bit more.  I really like the angle of the two large branches, and the way he''s looking right at you.  I might also experiment with some dodging and burning to see about setting him apart and making the eyes pop a bit more.<br/> <br/>All that being said, I really like it just the way it is as well!</td>', 'What a great capture of this guy!  How close were you?  I would have cropped it vertically and blurred the background some to isolate the owl a bit more.  I really like the angle of the two large branches, and the way he''s looking right at you.  I might also experiment with some dodging and burning to see about setting him apart and making the eyes pop a bit more. All that being said, I really like it just the way it is as well!', '2004-12-23 21:52:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1193188, 52398, 8367, '<td valign="top">Beautiful tones. I''m with you on this crop. I see it as horizontal thirds. It seems more symmetric and balanced to me. Great job and I''m glad you took the high road!</td>', 'Beautiful tones. I''m with you on this crop. I see it as horizontal thirds. It seems more symmetric and balanced to me. Great job and I''m glad you took the high road!', '2005-02-24 18:08:56.000000', NULL, 0),
